\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces One development series, \texttt  {ucr\_001}, under configuration (g). (a)~the training segment is cut chronologically into five client shards of $10/10/20/20/30\%$ plus a validation tail (v); the test segment and its labels are shared and never seen in training. (b)~each client's per-timestep score, its own train-fitted threshold (dashed), the timesteps it declares anomalous (tinted) and the single location it returns under the archive protocol (marker): all five agree, inside the labelled event, while their thresholds admit $1.2$ to $4.1\%$ of the test timesteps. (c)~the same event with the explanation, built with \emph  {no label in the loop}: the timesteps above client~1's threshold are masked across frequency, resampled from the prior with the remaining tokens as context and decoded locally (band = five draws, solid = median). Every configuration already localizes this series.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{2}{4}{One development series, \texttt {ucr\_001}, under configuration (g). (a)~the training segment is cut chronologically into five client shards of $10/10/20/20/30\%$ plus a validation tail (v); the test segment and its labels are shared and never seen in training. (b)~each client's per-timestep score, its own train-fitted threshold (dashed), the timesteps it declares anomalous (tinted) and the single location it returns under the archive protocol (marker): all five agree, inside the labelled event, while their thresholds admit $1.2$ to $4.1\%$ of the test timesteps. (c)~the same event with the explanation, built with \emph {no label in the loop}: the timesteps above client~1's threshold are masked across frequency, resampled from the prior with the remaining tokens as context and decoded locally (band = five draws, solid = median). Every configuration already localizes this series}{figure.2}{}}
